        "end_token_index": 230,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 231,
        "step_number": 3,
        "text": "Step 3: Analyze the composition \\( f(g(f(g(f(x))))) \\).\n- Start from the innermost function and work outward.\n- Let \\( y = f(g(f(x))) \\). We need to determine if \\( f(g(y)) \\) is even, odd, or neither when \\( y \\) is replaced by \\( -y \\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 980,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 982,
        "char_start": 666,
        "effective_step": 4,
        "end_token_index": 362,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 363,
        "step_number": 4,
        "text": "Step 4: Substitute \\( -x \\) into the expression.\n- Consider \\( f(g(f(g(f(-x))))) \\).\n- Since \\( f(x) \\) is odd, \\( f(-x) = -f(x) \\), so \\( f(g(f(-x))) = f(g(-f(x))) \\).\n- Since \\( g(x) \\) is even, \\( g(-f(x)) = g(f(x)) \\), thus \\( f(g(f(-x))) = f(g(f(x))) \\).\n- Therefore, \\( f(g(f(g(f(-x))))) = f(g(f(g(f(x))))) \\)."
